## Signature

- Provided by: **Claude Opus 5 (anthropic/claude-opus-5)** — 2026-10-08
- Method: fresh public internet research only — Google Cloud's **Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform model reference** for `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`, which supplied the model ID, the **2026-10-20 retirement notice**, the positioning statement, the full per-modality input/output matrix (text in and out; image, audio and video input only), the 1,048,576-token context and 65,536-token output limits, and the capability matrix (thinking, system instructions, structured output, implicit and explicit context caching, RAG Engine, tuning); and Google's **developer blog of 2025-06-17** for the preview introduction, the "lowest latency and cost in the 2.5 model family" positioning, the thinking-off-by-default design, the native tool list (Grounding with Google Search, Code Execution, URL Context, function calling), the high-throughput classification/summarization use case, and the explicit "requires less model intelligence" framing. Negative checks performed and reported: **BenchLM** (no entry, while Gemini 2.5 Pro, 2.5 Flash, 3.1 Flash-Lite and 3.5 Flash-Lite are all indexed); **evals.report** (404, while Gemini 1.5 Pro and 2.0 Flash resolve with 14 and 22 scores); **Artificial Analysis** (no entry); and a targeted benchmark search returning "No results found". Google's chart-only benchmark figure was deliberately **not** estimated. This folder's `meta.json` was read only to identify the tracked model; its OpenCode Zen free-tier claim is reported as **incorrect** against Zen's published catalogue. **No benchmark was imported from `gemini-2.5`, `gemini-2.5-flash` or `gemini-2.5-pro`**, each of which has its own folder and all of which Google positions above this tier. No peer `model/` findings files were read. Unavailable items — every benchmark figure, the knowledge cutoff, the architecture and the per-token price — are recorded as "no verified public data found" rather than estimated.
- Future sources: add a new file next to this one, e.g. `GPT_5.md`, using the same headings.
